/-!
# Vanishing of `H²` for congruence subgroups `Γ₀(M)` when `6` is a unit

The Sanov subgroup of `SL(2, ℤ)`, generated by `!![1, 2; 0, 1]` and `!![1, 0; 2, 1]`, is free
of rank two and contains `Γ(4)`. So `Γ₀(M) ∩ Γ(4)` (in Lean, `(Gamma 4).subgroupOf (Gamma0 M)`)
is a subgroup of a free group, hence free by Nielsen–Schreier, and its index in `Γ₀(M)` divides
the index of `Γ(4)` in `SL(2, ℤ)`, which divides `|SL(2, ℤ/4ℤ)| = 48`. Restriction to a free
subgroup kills `H²`, and corestriction composed with restriction is multiplication by the index.
Since the index divides `48` and `6` is a unit, `2` and hence the index are units, so
`H²(Γ₀(M), A)` vanishes for every representation `A`.
-/

namespace Gamma0H2

set_option autoImplicit false

